<td id="S4.T2.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">NABLA(0.4)</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><span id="S4.T2.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">42.08</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">85.02</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">75.76</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right">83.17</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">NABLA(0.2)+STA(11,24,24)</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">41.98</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">85.03</td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T2.5.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">76.04</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T2.5.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">83.22</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Human Evaluation</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conducted a side-by-side human evaluation comparing generated video quality obtained by the baseline model and the finetuned models across various configurations. 50 participants evaluated 20 video pairs each comparing videos on three key perceptual dimensions (prompt alignment, visual quality, dynamics) selecting one option per dimension: left is better, right is better, both are good, both are bad. Results in Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.2 Human Evaluation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ ∇NABLA: Neighborhood Adaptive Block-Level Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> show NABLA’s perceptual parity with baseline even at high sparsity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Human evaluation results (SBS test). NABLA maintains perceptual quality comparable to baseline at <math id="S4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80\text{\,}\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>80</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80\text{\,}\%</annotation></semantics></math> sparsity.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T3.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Judge</td>
